    "assumptions": [
      "Plan date is chosen in the product; the sample uses 2026-10-14, so the summer motorbike rule is off.",
      "Road distance is straight-line distance x 1.4. A public routing service only draws the line on the map, and never changes times, distance, or cost.",
      "Salik tolls are ignored.",
      "Each driver makes one trip per day, and a vehicle is not shared between shifts.",
      "Working time runs from the driver's shift start.",
      "Declared weight is for the whole consignment; dimensions are per piece.",
      "A driver who arrives early waits for the slot; lateness is judged by when delivery begins.",
      "Unknown stop types use the apartment time and are marked as guesses.",
      "Sharjah and Ajman deliveries are planned but flagged.",
      "The booked slot wins over a conflicting note, and the conflict goes to customer service.",
      "Addresses use past deliveries first, then OpenStreetMap geocoding with four checks, then the customer. Sahra is fictional, so few of its buildings can be geocoded.",
      "WhatsApp confirmations are shown as triggered but not sent, and Makani lookup is not connected.",
      "A parcel with a rough location is planned with a driver call if the customer has not replied by planning time. One with no location moves to tomorrow.",
      "The plan generator keeps to every limit. The hub manager has the final call, and any alerts at approval are saved and exported."
